@startuml frontend_product_boundary
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java dfb90cac4e233e09a0b8f047f7e9f4682f5ad238.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/App.vue submit; frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts sendMessage, dispatchSseFrame.
' Observed behavior: the internal workbench still consumes legacy Runtime request-scoped SSE and separate controls.
' Contract baseline: design 2ee2a3211da68ad87b0d9cab353e691b00bdaebd.
' Contract references: public-chat-alignment.md section 1, relative to this topic.
' Target-only architecture: product integration through Mate; no direct Runtime fallback.
' Design reason: public identity, protocol, and data visibility do not equal the internal transport.
title Product boundary - target-only integration
left to right direction
actor "User" as User
rectangle "Product browser" {
  component "Chat workspace\nno credential forms" as Workspace
  component "Public Chat Gateway" as Gateway
  component "Safe event reducer" as Reducer
}
rectangle "Host and Mate boundary" {
  component "Host identity transport\nintegration gate" as Host
  component "Public Chat API\nPOST JSON / GET live / GET history" as Mate
  component "Authorization and\nChat / Session mapping" as Mapping
  component "Safe event and\nhistory bridge - gate" as Bridge
}
rectangle "Internal Runtime - target contract" {
  component "Session API\nPOST SSE / GET numeric pages" as Runtime
}
User --> Workspace
Workspace --> Gateway
Gateway --> Host
Host --> Mate
Mate --> Mapping
Mapping --> Runtime
Runtime --> Bridge : committed events and preview
Bridge --> Mate : explicit public projection
Gateway --> Reducer : validated receipt, live, history
Reducer --> Workspace : immutable view
note bottom of Mate
Keep public and internal contracts separate.
Target correlation, tool result projection,
history snapshot bridging, and authentication
must be verified before production enablement.
end note
@enduml

@startuml frontend_debug_header_flow
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java 320d790726a70aada6100052952d5494d2a378ac.
' Reviewed implementation commit: pi-mono-java d03c08dbae870f19eee8d4fa79a707185f7a26b5 (Draft PR 181).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/DevDiagnostics.vue lines 1-26.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/composables/useRuntimeApi.ts lines 139-155 and 480-497 (sendMessage and requestRaw).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeEventController.java lines 58-73 (submit).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/web/RuntimeRequestContext.java lines 45-50 (mateCredentials).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/common/client/HttpMateToolClient.java lines 93-190 and 298-373.
' Historical behavior at 320d7907: no editor; latest dfb90ca has a DEV-only memory editor in frontend/src/debugHeaders.ts and App.vue submit.
' Observed behavior: the source baseline captures three headers on event submission and also sends them on discovery requests.
' Reviewed implementation: access-token is captured, discovery is credentialless, and only Mate tool execute receives the execution snapshot.
' Observed at dfb90ca: initial-message headers exist; new control and Skill request adapters remain target-only.
' Security hardening: browser validation, memory-only values, event-only request scope, redacted diagnostics, and no automatic POST replay.
' UI source evidence: pi-mono-java 4cc8dd86f601417c22cf9306e52152acbb59bb60 frontend/src/components/DebugHeaders.vue ensureTrailingRow, clearRows, template; frontend/src/debugHeaders.ts validateDebugHeaders.
' Observed UI: automatic blank rows and persistent explanatory prose. Target-only UI decision on 2026-09-09: optional editable presets, explicit Add, no persistent prose; legacy transport below is unchanged.
' Design reason: presets reduce typing; explicit Add avoids unwanted rows. Unused presets are omitted from validation, counts, and request snapshots.

title Internal debug header flow - legacy adapter scope
left to right direction

actor "Developer" as Developer

rectangle "Internal development frontend" as DevFrontend {
  component "Generic header table\nKey-value rows and inline validation" as Drawer
  component "In-memory enabled rows\nclear on reload" as HeaderState
  component "Event-only request adapter\nimmutable snapshot" as EventAdapter
}

rectangle "CampusClaw Runtime V1" as Runtime {
  component "POST sessions/{sessionId}/events\nRuntimeEventController.submit" as Submit
  component "RuntimeRequestContext\nexecution credential snapshot" as Snapshot
  component "Agent execution context" as Execution
}

rectangle "mate-service" as Mate {
  component "Agent, Skill, and tool metadata\ndiscovery without credentials" as Discovery
  component "POST runtime/tools/{toolId}/execute\ncredential headers attached" as Execute
}

Developer --> Drawer : edit temporary rows
Drawer --> HeaderState : update valid rows or clear
HeaderState --> EventAdapter : snapshot on message submit
EventAdapter --> Submit : initial event POST only
Submit --> Snapshot : capture request headers
Snapshot --> Execution : immutable for this execution
Execution --> Discovery : discover tools
Execution --> Execute : invoke a selected tool

note bottom of Drawer
Editable presets: access-token, X-HW-ID, Authorization.
Add one blank row on click; delete may leave no rows.
Generated headers are not rendered.
Manual values override generated values.

Reject invalid header tokens and CR/LF values.
Reject case-insensitive duplicate custom names.
Reject Fetch-forbidden request header names.
Show errors only on the affected row.
end note

note bottom of EventAdapter
Never attach the debug snapshot to:
- Session create, read, or delete
- History, model, or thinking
- Legacy control paths (now retired)

New Events control headers require a separate adapter.
This legacy allowlist is not the v2 contract.

Do not replay the event POST after disconnect.
end note

note bottom of Runtime
Runtime transport behavior:
- Capture values without authenticating them
- Do not persist values in Session or events
- Later edits affect only the next execution
- Recognize credential fields by the backend contract
end note

note bottom of Mate
Reviewed feature implementation:
- Discovery receives no credential snapshot
- Tool execute receives recognized credential values
- Missing required values fail before outbound call
- Logs and errors show presence only
end note
@enduml

@startuml assistant_rich_text_rendering
' Source baseline: pi-mono-java bde123706305a41e51c9a47b22e6ad11bbd8204c.
' Historical evidence below; dfb90ca frontend/package.json already includes markdown-it.
' Target decision: reuse the parser with a public content policy, not raw debugger visibility.
' Source evidence: frontend/src/components/ConversationTimeline.vue lines 37-49 (assistant text interpolation).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/projectors/runtimeEventProjector.ts lines 40-55 (projectAssistantEvent) and 133-145 (text extraction).
' Source evidence: frontend/src/style.css lines 784-789 (.assistant-message plain pre-wrap styling).
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEventProjector.java lines 149-176 and 215-238.
' Source evidence: modules/coding-agent-cli/src/main/java/com/campusclaw/codingagent/runtimeapi/event/RuntimeEntryCodec.java lines 67-88, 195-210, 430-442, and 557-601.
' Observed behavior: assistant text is preserved across delta, completed entry, SSE, and history but the current Vue component renders it as plain text.
' Target-only design: the Markdown parser, safe AST policy, Vue rich-text components, and rendering budget are not implemented at this baseline.
' Security hardening: raw HTML, remote Markdown images, relative application routes, and dangerous URL schemes never become active DOM.
' Design reason: use one raw Markdown source and one renderer so streaming, completion, and history recovery converge to equivalent UI.

title Assistant safe rich-text rendering - public integration target
top to bottom direction

rectangle "Validated public event input" as Input {
  component "agent.message phase=delta\ncontent fragment" as Delta
  component "agent.message phase=completed\nfull persistent content" as Completed
  component "GET history\nfull persistent text" as History
}

rectangle "Conversation projection" as Projection {
  component "Assistant turn\nrawMarkdown and state" as Raw
  component "Stable block boundary\nplus escaped streaming tail" as Stable
}

rectangle "Safe rich-text renderer" as Renderer {
  component "Markdown parser\nraw HTML disabled" as Parser
  component "AST allowlist\nURL policy and render budget" as Policy
  component "Fixed Vue components\nno v-html or innerHTML" as Vue
}

rectangle "Assistant message UI" as UI {
  component "Paragraphs, headings,\nlists, and quotes" as Prose
  component "Scrollable semantic table" as Table
  component "Inline code and code block\nwith text-only copy" as Code
  component "Safe external link" as Link
  component "Escaped plain-text fallback" as Fallback
}

Delta --> Raw : append source text
Completed --> Raw : replace preview with authority
History --> Raw : restore the same source text
Raw --> Stable : throttle while streaming
Stable --> Parser : stable blocks and safe tail
Parser --> Policy : Markdown AST
Policy --> Vue : allowed nodes and attributes
Policy --> Fallback : rejected or over budget
Vue --> Prose
Vue --> Table
Vue --> Code
Vue --> Link

note bottom of Input
Historical source and target policy:
- Source carries text, not HTML
- Target completed/history are authoritative
- Target tool and summary use plain text
end note

note bottom of Renderer
Security rules:
- Escape raw HTML
- Allow only absolute HTTP and HTTPS links
- Block Markdown image network requests
- Clamp heading levels inside the message
- Preserve source text for fallback and copy
end note

note bottom of UI
Responsive behavior:
- Only table and code containers scroll horizontally
- The page and composer never gain horizontal overflow
- Screen readers are notified once on completion
end note
@enduml

